---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { CORDEL_PLAY } from '../data/projects';

// Every fact on this page comes from the canonical project record. Nothing about components,
// contents, price, shipping or availability is written inline, so this page cannot drift away
// from what the company actually claims elsewhere.
const record = CORDEL_PLAY;
---

<Layout
  title="Cordel Play | ByteLite LLC"
  description="Cordel Play is a consent-first adult board game from ByteLite LLC. Product design is complete; manufacturing is in preparation. No retail release date has been announced."
  keywords="Cordel Play, adult board game, consent-first, ByteLite LLC"
  canonical="https://www.thebytelite.com/cordel-play/"
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product &middot; 18+</p>
      <h1>Cordel Play</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">{record.shortDescription}</p>
      <p class="age-gate">
        This is an adult product. It is intended for people aged 18 or over.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Design renders of finished component designs, deliberately labelled as such. There is no
       photography of a manufactured unit, because nothing has been manufactured - presenting a
       render as a product photo would be exactly the fabricated finished-product claim this site
       exists to avoid. The board render is NOT published: it carries a nude line figure, and this
       page is publicly indexed and reached from a company site whose other audience is enterprise
       licensing. The components below say what the game is without it. -->
  <section class="section-sm">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <figure class="fig">
        <img
          src="/cordel/cordel-play-tier-deck-backs-final.webp"
          alt="The seven Cordel Play card backs, left to right: Initiate, Connect, Seduce, Stimulate, Edge, Climax and Decree."
          width="1400" height="268" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>Six escalation tiers plus the Decree deck. Players choose how far the evening goes.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="fig fig-narrow">
        <img
          src="/cordel/cordel-play-consent-cup-final.webp"
          alt="The Cordel Play Consent Cup: a black lidded cup with a viewing dome, shown next to a cutaway view of the tokens inside."
          width="1000" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>The Consent Cup. Consent is a physical component of the game, not a rule someone has to remember.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="render-note">
        These are renders of the finished component designs. Nothing has been manufactured yet, so
        there is no photography of a real unit to show you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>What it is.</h2>
      <p class="body">{record.mission}</p>

      <h2 class="mt">Where it actually is.</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>{record.status}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Availability</dt><dd>{record.availability}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Next milestone</dt><dd>{record.nextMilestone}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Validation focus</dt><dd>{record.validationFocus}</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <h3 class="mt">Done</h3>
      <ul class="list">
        {record.currentCapabilities.map((c) => <li>{c.label}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h3 class="mt">Not done</h3>
      <ul class="list list-open">
        {record.inDevelopment.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt">The honest limitations.</h2>
      <ul class="list list-limit">
        {record.validation.map((v) => <li>{v.text}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The commercial rule that governs this product. It is a legal constraint, not a preference,
       so it is stated on the product page and not buried in terms. -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Why you cannot buy it here.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Cordel Play is a physical product in a box. It is not a subscription and will never be sold
        as one.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        I am not taking paid preorders for it. Under the FTC Mail, Internet, or Telephone Order
        Merchandise Rule, taking your money means committing to ship within a stated time, or
        within 30 days if no time is stated, and having a real process for getting your consent or
        refunding you when that slips. There is no approved shipment date, no approved price and no
        approved refund process yet, so there is nothing here I could honestly charge you for.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        You can register interest without paying anything. That records that you want it and locks
        the founder benefit. It stores no payment method and takes no money.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/founder-access" class="btn btn-primary">Register interest &mdash; no charge</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-outline">Ask me about it</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
.narrow { max-width: 780px; }
.page-hero { padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem; }
.hero-sub { max-width: 640px; font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-top: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; }
.age-gate {
  display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.25rem;
  font-size: .8125rem; font-weight: 600;
  color: #fbbf24; background: rgba(251,191,36,.08); border: 1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.3);
  border-radius: .5rem; padding: .5rem .875rem;
}
.fig { margin: 0 0 2rem; }
.fig img {
  display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem; background: #0d1120;
}
.fig-narrow { max-width: 520px; }
.fig figcaption { margin-top: .75rem; font-size: .875rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.6; }
.render-note {
  font-size: .8125rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;
  border-left: 3px solid #fbbf24; padding-left: .875rem;
}
h2 { margin-bottom: .75rem; }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin-bottom: .625rem; }
.mt { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
.body { font-size: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem; }
.facts {
  margin: 1.25rem 0 0; padding: 1.5rem;
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem;
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem 2rem;
}
@media (max-width: 560px) { .facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.facts dt { font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #555e7a; }
.facts dd { margin: .2rem 0 0; font-size: .9375rem; color: #e4e7f2; }
.list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .5rem; }
.list li {
  font-size: .9375rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.65;
  padding: .625rem .875rem; background: #0d1120;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #34d399; border-radius: .5rem;
}
.list-open li { border-left-color: #fbbf24; }
.list-limit li { border-left-color: #f472b6; }
.cta-row { display: flex; gap: .75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
</style>
